-- A BOOLEAN rule written as DECIDE clauses, one of which calls another rule,
-- beside the CONSIDER a drafter would write by hand. `l4 verify` reads the
-- group as the CONSIDER it stands for, so it counts the same atoms in both and
-- reads the call through in both.
DECLARE Peril IS ONE OF Water, Fire, Cosmetic

GIVEN x IS A BOOLEAN
      y IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `both hold` x y IS x AND y

GIVEN p IS A Peril
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE paid Water a b IS `both hold` a b
DECIDE paid p     a b IS a OR b

GIVEN p IS A Peril
      a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid by hand` p a b IS CONSIDER p
  WHEN Water THEN `both hold` a b
  OTHERWISE a OR b
